; The mark the meteor leaves on the floor while it is on its way.
;
; A thing in the world rather than a hint on the caster's screen, and that is
; the whole design: the client draws whatever the world holds, so the warning
; costs no client code, shows in a replay, and is hidden by the fog exactly as
; anything else is. No Body and no Geometry, like an arrow -- nothing shoots at
; it and nothing walks into it; it is a place, not an obstacle.
;
; How long it marks the ground and how hard it lands are the skill's, not its
; own: see the R skill of the Mage.
Projectile
  Name = MeteorMark
  DisplayName = Meteor
  VisionRange = 0
  Modules = [
    FallingUpdate
    End
  ]


; The mark the meteor leaves while it is falling, and then the meteor.
;
; It is an object in the world, so it is drawn here like anything else in
; flight -- which is the whole reason the warning cost no client code. Its
; effect, Meteor, lays a MARK as wide as the blast on the floor while it
; falls, and bursts where it lands.
  ; On the floor rather than at shot height: it is a place, not a thing passing.
  Height = 1
  Tint = 0xFF5A2A
  Effect = Meteor
  EffectOffset = 0
End
